      "writtenOn": "2017-02-20T06:35:47Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "the condition will be evaluated to false when a vndk_ext_library{...} exists but didn\u0027t set \u0027extends\u0027 attribute.\n\nThis is not an error. There are two types of vndk_ext library.\n\n1) by extending existing AOSP VNDK library (such as libbase). In this case, \u0027extends: \u003cexisting_vndk_lib_name\u003e\u0027.\n\n2) when a non-AOSP library need to be a VNDK library. In this case, \u0027extends\u0027 attribute should not set (because it is not extending any existing lib)\n\nI slightly modified the if-else structure and added comments to be clear on this.",
